IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nmw-types`

-- National Minimum Wage Act 1998 (UK) — GOAL 2: ARREARS (s 17).
--
--   "For a pay reference period in which the worker was paid less than the
--    national minimum wage, how much additional remuneration are they
--    entitled to at the time of determination?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1998-39.txt — ss 1(1), 17.

§ `Goal 2 — arrears`

-- s 17(1) "If a worker who qualifies for the national minimum wage is
-- remunerated for any pay reference period by his employer at a rate which
-- is less than the national minimum wage". The rate is the hourly rate of
-- remuneration under the s 2 regulations; read as remuneration divided by
-- hours, being less than the rate is remuneration below rate × hours.
@ref ss 1(1), 17(1)
GIVEN p IS A `Pay reference period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `was paid less than the national minimum wage` p IF
    p's `relevant remuneration received` LESS THAN `the remuneration at the national minimum wage for` p

GIVEN p IS A `Pay reference period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the remuneration at the national minimum wage for` p MEANS
    p's `rate payable during the period` TIMES p's `hours of work`

-- s 17(2) "the difference between— (a) the relevant remuneration received by
-- the worker for the pay reference period; and (b) the relevant remuneration
-- which the worker would have received for that period had he been
-- remunerated by the employer at a rate equal to the national minimum wage."
@ref s 17(2)
GIVEN p IS A `Pay reference period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shortfall A for` p MEANS
    `the remuneration at the national minimum wage for` p MINUS p's `relevant remuneration received`

-- s 17(4) "the amount determined by the formula— A/R1 × R2" (the formula is
-- lost in the conversion; this is its printed form). "R1 is the rate of
-- national minimum wage which was payable in respect of the worker during the
-- pay reference period, and R2 is the rate of national minimum wage which
-- would have been payable in respect of the worker during that period had the
-- rate payable in respect of him during that period been determined by
-- reference to regulations under section 1 and 3 above in force at the time
-- of determination."
@ref s 17(4)
GIVEN p IS A `Pay reference period`, r2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the uprated amount for` p `at the rate` r2 MEANS
    `the shortfall A for` p DIVIDED BY p's `rate payable during the period` TIMES r2

-- s 17(1) "whichever is the higher of— (a) the amount described in
-- subsection (2) below, and (b) the amount described in subsection (4)
-- below." (6) "Where any additional remuneration is paid ... but subsection
-- (1) above has not ceased to apply ..., the amounts described in subsections
-- (2) and (4) above shall be regarded as reduced by the amount of that
-- remuneration."
@ref s 17(1), (6)
GIVEN p IS A `Pay reference period`, r2 IS A NUMBER, paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the entitlement for` p `at the rate` r2 `after payments of` paid MEANS
    max (`the shortfall A for` p) (`the uprated amount for` p `at the rate` r2) MINUS paid

-- s 17(5) "Subsection (1) above ceases to apply to a worker in relation to
-- any pay reference period when he is at any time paid the additional
-- remuneration for that period to which he is at that time entitled under
-- that subsection." Each payment is tested against the entitlement at the
-- time it was made (with R2 as it then stood); a payment of at least that
-- entitlement ends the matter for the period.
@ref s 17(5), (6)
GIVEN p IS A `Pay reference period`, payments IS A LIST OF `Payment of arrears`
      paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the payments so far, unless paid in full, for` p `of` payments `after` paid MEANS
    CONSIDER payments
    WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST paid
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   x's `amount paid` AT LEAST `the entitlement for` p `at the rate` (x's `rate for the period under the regulations then in force`) `after payments of` paid
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE `the payments so far, unless paid in full, for` p `of` rest `after` (paid PLUS x's `amount paid`)

@ref s 17
@export The additional remuneration a worker is entitled to for one pay reference period under s 17 of the National Minimum Wage Act 1998 (UK) at the time of determination: if paid less than the national minimum wage, the higher of the shortfall A and A divided by the rate then payable (R1) times the rate that would be payable under the regulations in force at the time of determination (R2), less any additional remuneration already paid; nothing once it has been paid in full at any time (s 17(5)); nothing if the worker was not underpaid. Assumes the worker qualifies (s 1(2)). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Pay reference period`  @desc The hours of work and relevant remuneration under the s 2 regulations, the national minimum wage rate payable in the period (R1), and the payments of additional remuneration already made, each with R2 as it stood when paid
      r2 IS A NUMBER  @desc R2: the rate that would have been payable for the period under the regulations in force at the time of determination
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the additional remuneration for` p `at the time of determination, rate` r2 MEANS
    IF `was paid less than the national minimum wage` p
    THEN CONSIDER `the payments so far, unless paid in full, for` p `of` (p's `payments of additional remuneration`) `after` 0
         WHEN NOTHING     THEN 0
         WHEN JUST paid   THEN max 0 (`the entitlement for` p `at the rate` r2 `after payments of` paid)
    ELSE 0

@ref s 17
GIVEN periods IS A LIST OF `Underpaid period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the additional remuneration for all of` periods MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN u YIELD `the additional remuneration for` (u's `the period`) `at the time of determination, rate` (u's `rate for the period at the time of determination`)) periods)
